  "details": "The current shaders for Quest are quite outdated, as they were made for the Quest 1, and have not recieved any updates since then, and it heavily stifles what can be done on Quest worlds and Avatars. Issues with optimization exist, yes, which could be fixed by a toggle or something of the sort to allow custom shaders. With this, having a warning, saying it could potentially lag your game, and you may crash. But because of the limitations on Shaders, Quest users cannot see at least 50% of what can truly be done in VRChat.  It could allow for easier optimization, while also allowing the choice to Disable custom shaders in case you want better performance at the cost of heavily watered down Avatars and Worlds.",
